<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Blas de Lezo</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1689–1741</span> · <a href="/centuries/18th-century">18th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Blas de Lezo was a Spanish admiral from Pasajes in the Basque Country who had lost a leg, an eye and the use of an arm in earlier battles. As naval commander at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/cartagena-colombia">Cartagena de Indias</a> in 1741 he helped <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/viceroy-of-india">Viceroy</a> <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sebastian-de-eslava">Sebastián de Eslava</a> repel the large British expedition of Admiral <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/edward-vernon">Edward Vernon</a> during the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/war-of-jenkins-ear">War of Jenkins' Ear</a>, and died of illness a few months after the siege.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/blas-de-lezo.jpg" alt="Blas de Lezo" width="320" height="405" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Unidentified painter · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Don_Blas_de_Lezo_-Museo_Naval-.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
